2. CHANGES ARE WELCOME, ON TWO CONDITIONS
   You may modify Quillo, build on it, or use parts of it in your own software (together,
   a "Modified Version"). If you do, you must:

   a) Inform the author. Before you use a Modified Version or share it with anyone, tell
      the author by opening an issue in the Official Repository that says who you are,
      what you changed and why.

   b) Share it back. Upload the complete source code of your Modified Version to the
      Official Repository as a pull request (or, if that is not possible, attach it to the
      issue from (a)), under this same license, within 30 days of first using it.

   The author may include your changes in Quillo. You keep the credit for your own work.

3. KEEP THE CREDIT
   Every copy and every Modified Version must keep this license file, the copyright notice
   above, and the line "Quillo Community License · © 2026 Utkarsh Tripathi" at the bottom
